        "title": "Step 3: Early-Exit Lookup on PSL Monotonicity",
        "explanation": "Implement `get(key)` with early termination. Because Robin Hood insertion guarantees that any key with a larger `psl` would have displaced an occupant with a smaller `cur.psl`, if `cur === null || psl > cur.psl`, the target key cannot exist further down the probe chain.",
